WEBVTT

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.300
Hey,

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.190
Career Path Survey
Year:    Class:
Please tell us what occupation you'd like to do after graduating high school.
(Please fill in at least 2)
First Choice:
Second Choice:
Third Choice:

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.190
did you all fill this form out?

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:08.770
Career?

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.070
A manga artist!

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:11.650
What else would it be?

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.900
Meaning you didn't 
read the form properly.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.000
Career Path Survey
Year:    Class:
Please tell us what occupation you'd like to do after graduating high school.
(Please fill in at least 2)
First Choice:
Second Choice:
Third Choice:

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.000
You're supposed to at least 
write a second option.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.400
We were?

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.140
Yeah.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.140
What did you write, Ruki-chan?

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.440
Me?

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.340
My second choice is a 
nursery school teacher.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.430
Huh?

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:35.470
How could you leave Kaos behind 
to take care of other people's children?!

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.550
Yeah, yeah!

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.380
Pretty sure those are different things...

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:14.210
But why a nursery school teacher?

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.400
There aren't enough right now, 
so there's a demand for them,

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.680
and if I get my license, there'll be 
plenty of places I could apply to.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.670
Not to mention, I love kids.

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:25.800
You never know if you can make 
a living as a manga artist forever,

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.120
so I figure I should at least get a license.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.490
Knowing you,

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:31.370
you'd probably be able to do two jobs.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:32.730
Wow, Ruki-chan!

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:33.780
You're such a realist!

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.960
You'd be perfect as a nursery 
school teacher, Ruki-san.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.360
Right?

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.120
Not to mention, since I can draw,

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.750
we could draw together, too.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.180
Yeah, you probably shouldn't.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.680
What? But why?

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:49.180
Then maybe I'll work at a sweets shop.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.950
That's way too on a whim.

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:51.930
Nope.

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.940
My family actually runs a sweets shop.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.570
Welcome!

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.950
So that's why they always send you sweets.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:03.820
I'm the poster girl!

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:04.820
My...

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.650
My family also runs...

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.580
a small Japanese sweets shop...

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:13.130
Then we can totally make a 
western and Japanese sweets unit!

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:15.920
Things sure are getting exciting!

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.530
Aye!

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.000
Aye!

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:24.980
Is there... actually any demand for that?

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.280
Of course there is!

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.100
We could hold concerts and events,

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.320
and that'll make the shop prosper, too!

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:31.300
Right.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.100
You're still... going to draw manga, right?

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.310
Oh.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:38.100
So what are you going 
to write, Tsu-chan?

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.550
I have absolutely no interest in 
anything other than drawing manga.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.580
Of course you'd say that.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:45.090
I mean, we're just doing this 
for the sake of filling it out.

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:48.450
You could just put down
your father's company—

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.450
Career Path Survey
Year:    Class:
Please tell us what occupation you'd like to do after graduating high school.
(Please fill in at least 2)
First Choice:
Second Choice:
Third Choice:

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.830
I refuse to do everything 
my mother wants me to do!

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:53.700
Tsu-chan?!

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:57.170
Sorry, that just came out.

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:04.580
A-Are you okay? 
Actually, I should apologize...

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.430
It does seem that your mom

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:09.890
wants you to quit being a manga artist 
and take over the family business.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.130
Even though I wouldn't mean it,

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:13.800
I don't want to write something 
that'd make her happy.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.280
Even if it's just to fill out the form,

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.110
I'll actually consider 
something I might like to do.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:21.240
Right... Is there anything you can think of?

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:23.540
Yeah... A few things.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.860
Of course, I've always dreamed of being a hero,

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:28.950
but thinking realistically,

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:32.950
I need to find and train under a master 
so I can become a swordsman.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:35.120
Then I'll inherit their secret technique—

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.760
Tsu-chan! You can't think about this all by yourself!

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:39.460
As for me—

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:42.550
How long have you been there?!

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:45.910
Since something about a Japanese 
and Western sweets unit?

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:47.390
That's way towards the beginning!

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:53.040
I also put being a caregiver 
for my second option.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.100
There are plenty of places 
I could work at back home.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:00.820
So you're thinking seriously about your future.
What a surprise.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:01.900
Oh, I was kidding.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:05.870
I actually want to be the scariest 
ghost possible in the future!

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:08.080
Run!

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:12.900
You don't want people to think 
you're a proper person?

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:17.460
Career Path Survey
Year:    Class:
Please tell us what occupation you'd like to do after graduating high school.
(Please fill in at least 2)
First Choice:
Second Choice:
Third Choice:

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:17.450
What should I do?

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:21.520
I'm starting to think that drawing 
manga is all that I can do.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:24.420
I'm worse off than you are, Tsubasa-san...

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.300
Unlike Koyume-chan,

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:32.460
I've never properly been able 
to help out at my family's sweets shop...

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:32.470
I did it again...

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.420
Nothing. I couldn't do a thing right.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:39.560
Could I get this,
and that...

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:35.930
Mo—

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:39.550
And I've basically done nothing 
other than make my mom worry...

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.560
Mom!!

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:41.780
I'm the worst at drawing manga here

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:44.000
yet I'm the one who's holding 
onto manga the hardest!

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.810
I'm so pathetic!

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:47.230
Kaos...

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:51.090
Are you talking about your career paths?

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:52.720
Matron...

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.220
Here you are.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.290
Thank you very much.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:02.580
Thank you.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.300
It's a tough decision, isn't it?

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.680
I thought long and hard about it,

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.060
and ended up choosing 
not to be a manga artist.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:13.430
Huh?

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:15.860
I may not look it,

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:18.270
but I was also a student 
writer back in the day,

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.940
just like you girls are now.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.390
Huh?

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:22.760
But you know how,

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:26.290
once you become a professional, 
you can't draw exactly how you want to?

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:31.410
Though it's a bit embarrassing to say that 
in front of professionals like yourselves...

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.450
Like how this story won't sell,

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:36.530
or the readers just 
wouldn't understand...

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.630
When that was all I could think about,

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:42.500
it just wasn't fun anymore.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:47.710
Hanabi

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:47.710
I did actually release a tankobon 
about seven years ago...

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:49.900
What was it called?

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.420
Oh, how embarrassing.

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:55.640
It was "The Afternoon 
Smells Like Oranges."

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:56.420
Huh?

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:59.410
You're Rika Sonoda-sensei?

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.640
Oh, you've actually 
heard of it, Kaos-chan?

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:02.960
Yes, yes!

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:05.910
I saw the name on a review site 
and I was really curious about this writer!

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:07.780
She was really popular,

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:10.000
but it's really hard to find her comics!

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:10.770
Look!

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:15.410
"So much potential!" 
"What an amazing talent."

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:17.080
Customer Review
5 Customer reviews 5 out of 5 stars
Top review 
Contributor: www
So much potential! I'm sure this 
author is going to sell and become even more popular.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:17.080
Contributor: cmg
My first thought was, "What an amazing talent."
I'm excited to see what they write next.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:17.090
"When's the next book coming out?"

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.140
Wow!

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:20.750
You still have so many fans!

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:21.540
Oh, stop.

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:25.500
But you see...

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:30.220
I wasn't able to meet all of these 
readers' expectations,

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:34.190
and I couldn't continue as a pro.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:36.880
You're all wonderful,

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:39.350
because you're actual professionals.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:43.300
Actual... professionals?

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:49.440
But I still love seeing manga artists 
working hard and mangas being made.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:55.630
That's why I figured I still wanted to be 
involved with manga in my own way.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:08:00.080
I feel like I understand 
your decision, Matron.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:02.720
Of course, I don't have any regrets.

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:04.710
This is my life, after all.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:07.800
And I still draw manga 
sometimes as a hobby.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:08.870
Huh.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:16.420
And that's why I want to do 
whatever I can to help all of you out.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.570
Um...

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:19.960
I have a request.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.250
What is it, Kaos-chan?

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:26.480
Could you show me the manga 
you're drawing as a hobby?

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.870
I want to see it, too, Ri-chan!

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:31.440
No way.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:32.740
What?!

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:34.550
Why?!

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:44.830
Moving out of the dorm 
Please do so by 2/2 (Sat)

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:44.830
I guess it's finally time...

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:50.680
It feels like only yesterday that 
Koyume-chan and Kaos-chan arrived.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:52.680
It went by so fast.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:58.560
I never thought we'd actually 
have to leave this dorm.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:04.470
So on this weekend, 
since none of you have deadlines,

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:07.280
I thought I'd have you help 
sort the storage room.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:08.320
Is that all right?

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:09.560
Yes, ma'am!

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.360
Good answer.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:15.400
The storage room has things that 
the other residents left behind.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.950
The storage room is straight ahead.

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.220
This is amazing.

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:35.220
Hey, this is a first edition.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:37.720
There are even rough sketches in color!

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.090
So many reference books!

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:41.520
Come on, now.

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:43.630
If you keep getting distracted 
by all the treasures down here

00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:45.090
we're never going to finish 
by the end of today.

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:49.390
Divide everything up in groups 
and put them into boxes.

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:50.730
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.690
This looks like it'd be really useful.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:16.070
I wonder if the matron would 
let me borrow it if I asked her.

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:17.000
Yes,

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.460
I believe she would.

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:26.290
U-Um...

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:27.620
Tsubasa-san...

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:28.480
Hm?

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:32.480
Did you fill out your career path survey?

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.480
Oh, that...

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:37.120
I wrote "manga artist" 
for my first and second choice.

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:41.740
I... see.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.250
What did you write, Kaos?

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:47.090
I still haven't filled mine out...

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:48.970
I see.

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:50.080
Of course,

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:53.040
I still want to continue working 
to become a manga artist.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:54.160
But...

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:58.750
When I think about whether I'm actually going 
to be able to continue walking down this path or not

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:00.170
I get so worried.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:04.140
I'd be lying if I said I wasn't worried.

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:05.940
But for now,

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:08.280
I'm just not thinking about that.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:12.230
I... see.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:14.580
I guess we should take this down.

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:15.530
It's pretty beat up.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:17.700
Yes, let's do that.

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:23.120
Should we keep this?

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:23.890
What is it?

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:24.820
Let me see.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.970
Of course...

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.430
Kaos?

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:47.550
Right, I'll keep working hard.

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:48.370
But...

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:51.270
you <i>have</i> been working 
hard cleaning up.

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:52.470
Yes.

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:55.030
I'm going to continue 
working even harder!

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:56.540
U-Um, sure...

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:58.020
Let's do our best.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:11.460
Moving out of the dorm 
Please do so by 2/2 (Sat)

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:24.370
Tighten your core even more!

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:27.050
What in the world are you doing?

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:31.060
Oh, I'm trying to get fired up, 
so I can escape rejection hell.

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:34.170
Oh... So that's what you were doing.

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:34.950
Yes.

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:35.970
Kaos-chan,

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:37.780
you're drawing up storyboards 
left and right, aren't you?

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:39.230
Yes!

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.130
Are you okay, Kaos-chan?

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:46.980
Yes.

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:49.130
Please go ahead and sleep, Koyume-chan.

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:54.400
Yeah, but before I go to sleep, I'm going to
make you something warm to drink.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:56.090
Thank you very much.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:02.720
I smell some yummy cocoa.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:05.650
I guess I'll make some cocoa, too.

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:07.680
Is Kaos-chan still at it?

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:08.830
Yeah!

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:11.060
She's determined to have 
her next storyboard accepted.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:16.990
Sorry it took so long, Kaos-chan.

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:19.370
Oh, thank you very much.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:28.160
I guess I'll work a little harder, too.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:29.420
Huh?

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:30.370
Right.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.180
Let's do our best together.

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:34.490
I'm going to draw a trash storyboard!

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:36.330
No, you're not supposed to do that!

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:43.440
Thank you for your time.

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:44.040
Of course.

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:44.780
Wait...

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:47.530
You brought four... at once?

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:48.300
Yes...

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:51.550
It's been almost a year 
since I moved into the dorm.

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:52.960
If I let things end like this,

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:55.510
I think my self-loathing 
is going to crush me.

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:57.560
I-I see...

00:13:57.990 --> 00:14:02.290
<i>It's truly amazing how hard Kaos-sensei 
works when she's pushed to the edge.</i>

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:04.780
I'll go ahead and take a look.

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:05.860
Please wait!

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:06.850
If you could,

00:14:06.850 --> 00:14:09.370
please look at these 
in order from best to worse!

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:11.920
You don't even have 
to look at the last one...

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:12.620
Um...

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.360
You could use them 
as oil blotting sheets!

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:16.300
Or write notes on the back.

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:17.820
Please stop struggling.

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:22.960
Let's start with the first one.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:30.220
There's someone 
I'm interested in.

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:25.620
Is this a romantic comedy?

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:30.220
Sorry!

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:26.560
Yes!

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:30.210
I never thought I'd see something like 
this come from you, Kaos-sensei.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:30.220
I'm a
bit late!

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:33.280
I talked with a shojo manga artist...

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:35.420
And with the art style...

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:39.610
I thought about what was charming 
about the male character when I drew it.

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:41.910
<i>The male character's charm?</i>

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:43.860
<i>As told by Kaos-sensei?</i>

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:45.230
<i>I wonder what...</i>

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.500
<i>Hup!</i>

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:48.070
Hup!

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:48.070
So
dreamy.

